{
  "family": "uniform-hypergraph",
  "canonical_name": "GTBase.hypergraph_uniformity.uniform_family",
  "canonical_short_name": "uniform_family",
  "relation": "Exact set-family uniformity: over an arbitrary finite vertex type T, every member e of E : {set {set T}} has #|e| = k (Prop), with the Boolean view [forall e in E, #|e| == k] reflected by uniform_familyP; the indexed adapter uniform_incidence inc k := forall i, #|inc i| = k equals uniformity of the image family without injectivity. No nonempty-family, positive-rank, loopless, no-isolated-vertex, carrier-inhabitance or partiteness guard; partite uniformity, complete-uniform/containment predicates and degree regularity are separate contracts.",
  "baseline_commit": "3be65eed7084abfae36dee74f7117b598325bc4c",
